<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gaspar de Guzmán, Count-Duke of Olivares</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1587">1587</a>–<a href="/years/1645">1645</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Count-Duke of Olivares, Olivares</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gaspar de Guzmán, Count-Duke of Olivares, was the chief minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-iv-of-spain">Philip IV of Spain</a> from 1621 to 1643. He sought to restore Spanish power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a> and to share its costs among all the king's realms through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-of-arms">Union of Arms</a>. His demands provoked the revolts of Catalonia and Portugal in 1640, and he fell from power in 1643.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gaspar-de-guzman-count-duke-of-olivares.jpg" alt="Gaspar de Guzmán, Count-Duke of Olivares" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Diego Velázquez · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Count-Duke_of_Olivares.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
